WEBVTT
NOTE smp12-a4-hillsborough en - the 1989 commentary subtitled (Review 1 #67, user 13 Nov); Arabic approved by the user 14 Nov

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.800
What you see: archive news footage from the day.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.800
1989 - Hillsborough, England: 97 people died after overcrowding in standing areas behind a goal.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.400
Archive commentary, 1989: We must go now to Hillsborough.

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.100
What looks to be a major incident there, Peter Jones.

5
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:19.000
The teams have just left the field. The trouble is away to our left, in a packed enclosure of Liverpool supporters.

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.400
Two and a half minutes after the match started, they came over the top of the fence.

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.500
Police are trying desperately hard to hold them back. At the moment it is simple mayhem.

8
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.900
The police just said: just go through, you open the gate, just go in - it doesn't matter about the tickets.

9
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.900
They didn't say who's got tickets and who hasn't. They just opened the gate to let anybody in.

10
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.600
We heard the policeman say: we've opened the gate - there's going to be people killed outside.

11
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.600
It was just like a mass relief.

